I have a couple comments about nethack as it stands(pl9 for me).
I used to play it quite a bit but have tapered it off because of
the unfairness of it.  Don't worry about me, I've got my flameproof
suit on.

Once you get a character to the castle level your character should
only die of ignorance, from which you learn, or because s/he got
overmatched somehow(rare).  One I can learn from, the other is
just the way it goes sometimes.

What I object to is stupid sudden death.  I don't know too many
people where I work that could make a living typing, death my
typing mistake should have no part of the game.  The ultimate
for me was a character that had everything I could think of 
except the Amulet of Lifesaving.  +8 Stormbringer, +8 Excalibur,
+7 Demonsbane, AC riduculus, everything I wanted except the 
amulet.  I learned how to teleport down to hell, walked around
the maze a bit, and fell into a moat I didn't see and had never
heard mentioned!  By the time a character gets to that level
he should get beaten, he shouldn't die a stupid sudden death.
And for those of you who are saying "You should have been wearing
this or have drank that" the game is too rich to do everything
at once.  I'd put floating eyes in the category of death by
typing mistake, the game doesn't need them.  Especially when
one has been at the keyboard for many hours.

Another stupid sudden death.  I find it impossible to imagine
anyone stupid enough to eat so much that s/he would choke to 
death.  Perhaps if there was an intristic to gain you could
force your character past safety, but not otherwise.  I have
had more characters than I care to think about choke to death
many turns after s/he had gotten sated eating something but
food was rare.

No character I invest more than 10 hours in should die like that.

Another thing that got me killed all to often when I was starting
out was my inability to get sleep resistance.  Our top 10 list
was full of my characters that got wiped out by Orange dragons.
Elves should not be something you get an intristic from, I consider
my characters "human" and the game frowns on cannibals.  If I 
found a barbarian and killed him would I get poison resistance?

Also, since I went to pl9 Excalibur seems to be a waste of time.
Is there anything I can do about that?  Currently I don't bother
with it.

marty


